# Tests

## Unit tests (core)

- JUnit 5 with `AemContextExtension`. Build content in the test with `context.create()` or JSON fixtures; for fragments use the `Fragments` fixture, which writes the same JCR shape the package installs.
- Name tests after behaviour (`tagsAllRequiresEveryTag`), and cover the empty, invalid and limit cases as well as the happy path.
- Don't mock what AEM Mocks provides (resources, ValueMaps, tags). Mock only OSGi services you own.
- JaCoCo fails the build below 80 % line coverage. Don't add exclusions to pass it.

## UI tests (ui.tests/test-module)

- Playwright with TypeScript. Import `test` and `expect` from `tests/fixtures.ts`, which adds the `consoleErrors` fixture.
- Navigate with `/content/...` paths: publish mapping is outbound only (ADR-026).
- Select by role, label or the component's BEM class. Never by generated IDs.
- Every new page state gets an axe scan (`wcag2a`, `wcag2aa`, `wcag21a`, `wcag21aa`). Serious or critical violations fail.
- Both projects (`mobile-375`, `desktop-1280`) must pass. Run `npm run lint` (tsc) before committing.
